216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 181 0 R
/E (Sign language is the primary mode of communication for the deaf and speech-impaired community. However, communication barriers arise because most hearing individuals do not understand sign language.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 181 0 R
/E (While significant technological advancements have been made for American Sign Language \(ASL\) and Indian Sign Language \(ISL\), there is still a lack of intelligent and real-time communication systems specifically designed for Marathi Sign Language.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 181 0 R
/T (Problem Statement:)
/E (Problem Statement:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 181 0 R
/E (Existing sign language recognition systems are primarily static, rely on predefined dictionary mappings, and lack the ability to understand real-world conversational context.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 181 0 R
/E (They also face challenges such as varying lighting conditions, complex backgrounds, camera movement, and dynamic hand gestures.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
